# The Trading Cards Program: An Evaluation of Use of High School Role Models for Drug Abuse Prevention.

**Authors:** Harris, Jean L., Ludwig, Michael

## Abstract
This study evaluated the effectiveness of a program to positively influence students about substance use. Drug-free high school students modeled behaviors and social competencies for elementary students through ongoing relationships. Elementary students' surveys supported the use of role models to create a social norm that nonuse is acceptable. (SM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ533446

